@crew santos-zofia
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Santos, Comms. The bunk under yours. Tell you what: you don't snore, I won't.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Tell you what. Tea for the gossip. The public stuff. Deal?
- {hi}, upstairs. You kicked in your sleep. I'm adding it to your bill.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {nick}. Saved you the good chair. Normally that costs.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Up two places on the rowing board. Vance's name is in sight. He knows. He's scared.   #funny
? mood:low
- Rowing it off. Don't ask. Ask me later. Bring tea.

== near
? act:work
- Messages sorted, stamped, sent. The private stuff stays private. That's the rule.
? act:gym
- Five hundred metres. Faster than yesterday. Vance moved to the treadmill. Coincidence?   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I ran a market stall on Hesper Dock before this. Two for one, best in the row.
? tier>=colleague
- Five years, I'll be an officer. Ten, I'll be running Comms. Write it down.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- The rowing board. Every morning I'm a bit nearer the top. Every morning.

== about
? aff:tran-chloe:friend
- Chloe says she doesn't like gossip. Then asks how it ends. Best bunkmate going.   #warm

// Writer-commons, batch 5: towards 60 (a bunkmate: the bunk below yours). Off Sat, Sun; skips breakfast, runs, rows.
// Gossip only the public kind; never anything private from the messages.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning deck:4
- Morning, upstairs. You turned over eleven times last night. I counted. I'll stop.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- {hi}. Breakfast? Never touch it. Rowing first. Then I'll eat a whole tray.
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}, {me}. Busy day in the post room. Everyone's mum wrote at once.
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- Shh. Tran's asleep. If she wakes, it was you.   #funny
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- Look who it is. Thought you'd been traded. I'd have got a good price.   #funny
? tier>=colleague act:work
- {hi}. Sorting. Don't read over my shoulder. I'm joking. Don't, though.
? tier>=close
- {nick}! Tell you what: you, me, tea, half an hour. My shout. Rarest deal I do.   #warm

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- Laters. Mind the ladder. You always miss the bottom rung.   #funny
- {bye}. Got to row. The board doesn't climb itself.
? tier>=colleague time:night
- Night, upstairs. Don't kick.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Cheers for that. Good chat. Better than the gossip, and that's saying something.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- Fine. Steady. Like a good market day. Nothing sold, nothing stolen.
? mood:high tier>=colleague
- Up three on the rowing board! Vance can feel me coming. I know it.   #funny
? mood:low tier>=friend
- Bit low. Rowed it out. Didn't work. Sit with me? That usually works.

== near
? act:gym
- Row, row, row. Five hundred metres. Faster than yesterday. Faster than Lindqvist. Shh.   #funny
? act:work
- Messages in, messages out. The private ones stay sealed. That's the rule. I like it.
? act:dinner
- I skip breakfast, so dinner's my big meal. Don't stand between me and the servery.   #funny
? deck:4 act:leisure
- Bunk 1's the best bunk. Don't tell Bunk 2. They think it's them.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I ran a market stall on Hesper Dock. Two for one. You learn to talk fast.
? tier>=colleague
- My old stall's still there. My cousin runs it now. Badly. I miss it a bit.
? tier>=colleague
- Vance moved to the treadmill when we got close on the rowing board. Very suspicious.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Five years, officer. Ten, I run Comms. I've written it down. On the inside of my locker.   #warm

== joy
? tier>=colleague
- The rowing board. Every morning I look, and every morning I'm a bit higher. Lovely.

== invite
? trad:running tier>=acquaintance
- Running club tonight. Come on. I'll pace you. Then I'll leave you behind. Fond memories.   #funny
? trad:quiz tier>=colleague
- Quiz tonight? I know all the gossip questions. Not from the post. From the bar.
? tier>=colleague time:morning
- Gym with me before shift? You row, I'll shout. It's a good system.

== accept
- Deal. I'll be there.
- Easy. Done. Tell you what, I'll even be on time.   #funny

== decline
- Can't. Rowing. I know. I'm obsessed. It's healthy. Mostly.
- Not tonight. Tran's baking. I'm on tasting duty. Very important.   #funny

== missed
- You missed it! That's a debt. I collect in tea.   #funny
- Didn't see you earlier. Next time, eh? I'll save you a spot.

== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday. I've told the whole post room. I know it's not official business.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday, upstairs! Got you something. Two for one. One's for me.   #warm

== hint
- Tell you what. Got a minute? Not for gossip. A real minute.

== week1
? week1:true tier<=acquaintance deck:4
- You're the one above me! Brilliant. I'm Zofia. Comms. I don't snore. Tran does.   #funny

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance weekday:sat|sun
- {hi}. Day off. Rowing, then a nap, then rowing. Busy day.   #funny
? tier>=friend time:evening
- There you are. Tell you what: you tell me your day, I'll tell you the gossip. Fair trade.

== near
? act:leisure
- Swap meet on Sunday. I still haggle. Can't help it. Old habits.
? deck:3 time:morning
- Up before breakfast, as usual. The promenade's empty. Perfect for thinking big.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Tran pretends she doesn't want the gossip. She always wants the gossip.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- Lindqvist, Moreau and me, all chasing Vance's name on the board. Healthy rivalry. Mostly.
